From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Cather <mattbob4@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:48:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: return NULL from the stubbed rfkill_init()

320-optional_rfkill.patch compiles rfkill out when CONFIG_RFKILL is unset
and has the stub rfkill_init() return (void *) 1. Both callers own the
struct rfkill_config they pass in and release it only when rfkill_init()
returns NULL, so the sentinel silently disables the only cleanup path.
The stubbed rfkill_deinit() frees nothing either, and nothing else ever
holds the config, so it leaks on every interface add.

NEED_RFKILL is referenced once in src/drivers/drivers.mak and never set,
so the stub is the only configuration that gets built.

Return NULL instead. That restores the contract for the callers in
driver_nl80211.c and driver_wext.c and makes the compiled-out path behave
like the already-exercised case where /dev/rfkill is simply absent.

Signed-off-by: Matthew Cather <mattbob4@gmail.com>
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/25339
[Crescentm: from OpenWrt PR #25339 head ab8903a1a3fc14df63e3dc064054d9a8a06e27fe,
 commit e90e3a2287, unchanged]
---
 .../services/hostapd/patches/320-optional_rfkill.patch       | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/320-optional_rfkill.patch b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/320-optional_rfkill.patch
index aeeaeb4331..bcee09cb79 100644
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/320-optional_rfkill.patch
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/320-optional_rfkill.patch
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@ Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: make rfkill support optional
  ifdef NEED_RADIOTAP
 --- a/src/drivers/rfkill.h
 +++ b/src/drivers/rfkill.h
-@@ -18,8 +18,24 @@ struct rfkill_config {
+@@ -18,8 +18,25 @@ struct rfkill_config {
  	void (*unblocked_cb)(void *ctx);
  };
  
@@ -49,7 +49,8 @@ Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: make rfkill support optional
 +#else
 +static inline struct rfkill_data * rfkill_init(struct rfkill_config *cfg)
 +{
-+	return (void *) 1;
++	/* callers release the config only on a NULL return */
++	return NULL;
 +}
 +
 +static inline void rfkill_deinit(struct rfkill_data *rfkill)

From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Cather <mattbob4@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:48:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: free the association frame taxonomy in
 ap_free_sta()

600-ubus_support.patch adds sta->assoc_frame_taxonomy beside hostapd's
own probe_ie_taxonomy and assoc_ie_taxonomy, and fills it with a
wpabuf_alloc_copy() of the association frame, but never extends the
CONFIG_TAXONOMY free block in ap_free_sta().

hostapd frees its own two there. Ours is only ever replaced, so the last
copy a station carried leaks when that station is freed on disassoc,
deauth or inactivity timeout, and the copy is the whole association
frame.

Free it beside the other two.

Signed-off-by: Matthew Cather <mattbob4@gmail.com>
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/25339
